    "html": "<p>A metal cylinder of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span> and specific heat capacity <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"c\"></span> is heated to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"90^{\\circ}\\mathrm{C}\"></span>. It is then submerged in an insulated container of liquid with mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2M\"></span> and specific heat capacity <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2c\"></span>. The initial temperature of the liquid is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"15^{\\circ}\\mathrm{C}\"></span>. Assuming no energy is lost to the surroundings, what is the final equilibrium temperature of the system?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"75^{\\circ}\\mathrm{C}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"30^{\\circ}\\mathrm{C}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"40^{\\circ}\\mathrm{C}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"52.5^{\\circ}\\mathrm{C}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
